    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d437">

                <pb facs="0423" n="409" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg409"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M)/7945: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Long</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-01T17:00:00-04:00">August 1, 1942—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>557. For Reynolds. Your 615, July 27 and 232, July 30.<anchor n="90"
                        xml:id="d437-f1"/> Substantial agreement has been reached with Kinnear and
                        Moore<anchor n="91" xml:id="d437-f2"/> along lines outlined by you. Certain
                    details remaining to be agreed upon are expected to be settled on Monday or
                    Tuesday. The only important variation from your plan is that Rubber Reserve may
                    make other contracts with respect to rubber in Ecuador after suitable notice to
                    the corporation, the amount of notice required now being under discussion.</p>
                <p>Question of management commissions not yet discussed. It is acceptable to BEW and
                    will be discussed with Kinnear on Monday.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d437-f1" n="90" xml:id="d437-f1-content">
                <p>Latter not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d437-f2" n="91" xml:id="d437-f2-content">
                <p>Ross E. Moore, Office of Foreign Agricultural Relations, Department of
                    Agriculture.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
